description:
The `content_restart()` function creates a new environment variable with a unique timestamp to trigger a restart of a content item. However, this _CONNECT_RESTART_{timestamp} env var does not get cleaned up appropriately. My expectation is that it should be removed. 

https://github.com/posit-dev/connectapi/blob/3291a968464a6dff4f0db4680edb5ac3aa060c73/R/content.R#L1436-L1437

I have a suite of applications across different posit connect instances that pull in new data daily and we recently switched to using `connectapi` from using the API directly via a CI/CD tool to dynamically warm these applications. The result is that each one of these content items (shiny apps / rmd reports), retains a CONNECT_RESTART env variable during each warming (every day). Which is leading to a large bloat of env variables for our content items.

reprex below.

```r
library(connectapi)

restart_connect_content <- function(server, api_key, guid) {
  conn <- tryCatch(
    connectapi::connect(server = server, api_key = api_key),
    error = function(e) e
  )
  if (inherits(conn, "error")) {
    return(list(
      ok = FALSE,
      error = sprintf("Cannot connect to instance: %s", conditionMessage(conn)),
      context = list(server = server, guid = guid)
    ))
  }

  item <- tryCatch(
    connectapi::content_item(conn, guid),
    error = function(e) e
  )
  if (inherits(item, "error")) {
    return(list(
      ok = FALSE,
      error = sprintf("Unable to retrieve content item %s: %s", guid, conditionMessage(item)),
      context = list(server = server, guid = guid)
    ))
  }

  rst <- tryCatch(
    {
      connectapi::content_restart(item)
      "ok"
    },
    error = function(e) e
  )

  if (identical(rst, "ok")) {
    message("Restart request sent.")
    return(list(ok = TRUE, error = NULL, context = list(server = server, guid = guid)))
  }

  msg <- conditionMessage(rst)
  if (grepl("(500|Internal Server Error)", msg, ignore.case = TRUE)) {
    warning(sprintf("content_restart returned 500, but this often indicates the app is restarting"))
    return(list(ok = TRUE, error = NULL, context = list(server = server, guid = guid)))
  }

  list(
    ok = FALSE,
    error = sprintf("Unexpected error during restart: %s", msg),
    context = list(server = server, guid = guid)
  )
}

# Setup
server <- "https://your-connect-server.com"
api_key <- Sys.getenv("CONNECT_API_KEY")
guid <- "your-app-guid-here"

# Simulate 7 daily restarts
for (day in 1:7) {
  restart_connect_content(server, api_key, guid)
  Sys.sleep(1)
}

# Check environment variable accumulation
client <- connect(server, api_key)
content <- content_item(client, guid)
env_vars <- content$environment_all()
restart_vars <- names(env_vars)[grepl("^_CONNECT_RESTART_", names(env_vars))]

cat(sprintf("Restart variables found: %d\n", length(restart_vars)))
print(restart_vars)
```

